R.append(scoped_record('c0809','cassini-solar-union','The Cassini Division — Solar Union','The Cassini Division','The moneyless nanotechnological human commonwealth',['book'],
 'Fall Revolution, Solar Union as depicted in The Cassini Division','Established Union before the closing interstellar military intervention','Living human and active human-derived Union residents',
 ['New Mars capitalist institutions','Non-cooperating money enclaves as Union beneficiaries on identical terms','All uploaded Jovian minds as Union citizens'],
 'The Solar Union uses nanotechnology to make ordinary material wealth readily available without money. The gathered review explicitly describes a guarantee extending across its citizens, rather than merely a wealthy protagonist with a private fabricator. Guarantees are rated strong within the established commonwealth, while destructive nanotechnology and the reviewer’s doubts about defensive resilience limit any claim of absolute security.\n\nOpen elected committees govern both ordinary institutions and the Cassini Division. Combined with common access to decisive productive technology, this supports control toward distributed human ownership, with a broad interval for the difference between formal participation and actual influence. The existence of capable computers does not establish independent AI sovereignty. Useful military, scientific, artistic and care activity continues, so freedom from money and subsistence employment is not treated as universal idleness. Human-derived active residents are a disclosed proxy, while hostile Jovian posthumans and separate money enclaves are not assigned the Union’s rights or institutions.',
 [-.85,.8,None],[[-1,-.35],[.5,1],None],
 ['The review explicitly connects nanotechnology to broadly guaranteed material wealth and a moneyless economy.','Open elected committees and broadly available productive capacity support distributed human control, with uncertainty about informal influence.',nw],refs,2,proxy=True))
