R.append(scoped_record('c0814','lady-mazes-teven-coronal','Lady of Mazes — Teven Coronal’s supported manifolds','Lady of Mazes','Shared nanotechnological support beneath culturally distinct manifolds',['book'],
 'Teven Coronal at the beginning of Lady of Mazes','Established coronal life before the external dismantling of manifolds','Living humans and active human-derived coronal residents',
 ['All perceived people as additional active persons','Every manifold as a separately counted economic order','Later Archipelago arrangements or invasion as unchanged provision'],
 'Teven’s residents inhabit distinct culturally curated manifolds while sharing an AI-built habitat and nanotechnological productive support. The gathered accounts describe ordinary goods, services and information as accessible without necessary work or payment. Guarantees are provisionally strong within the functioning coronal, with technology locks and dependence on shared infrastructure limiting any claim of unrestricted individual power. The invasion that dismantles these cultures is a separate condition.\n\nControl remains unresolved. Choosing or inhabiting a narrative environment does not necessarily confer ownership of its physical support, while AI assistance does not by itself prove that humans have no effective authority. The manifolds vary in visible technology and social customs, but this record counts their shared material model once until a concrete allocation difference warrants a split. Living humans and active human-derived residents form an explicit denominator; perception management is not assumed to turn everyone into a stored file. Cultural creation, diplomacy, care and technical work can continue, so nonworking remains null.',
 [-.7,None,None],[[-.95,.15],None,None],
 ['The named coronal’s nanotechnological habitat support and accessible goods/services are explicit in the labeled reviews.','Curated perceptions, local choices and AI assistance leave effective ownership of shared physical infrastructure unresolved.',nw],refs,1,proxy=True,alternatives=[5]))
refs=[P+'ventus']
R.append(scoped_record('c0815','ventus-winds-technological-ceiling','Ventus — Human society under the Winds’ ceiling','Ventus','Preindustrial humans within a machine-maintained ecosystem',['book'],
 'Ventus, established human settlements before the central mystery is resolved','The inherited preindustrial order under the Winds','Living human descendants of the colonists',
 ['The intended automated colony as fully implemented human access','The Winds’ ecosystem protection as a universal individual food floor','Later reconciliation as an already verified new economy'],
 'The Winds maintain a terraformed biosphere that would otherwise become poisonous, yet reject advanced human technology as an ecological threat. Human descendants therefore remain in preindustrial monarchies and aristocracies despite the surrounding nanotechnological capacity. This is an interpretive zero variant: machine restrictions retain ordinary human subsistence and craft labor. Ecological misrecognition, rather than a policy to preserve paid jobs, is the relevant cause.\n\nUltimate control over the technological ceiling lies with the autonomous Winds, near the machine-control end of the axis. Human local rulers retain power within that ceiling but cannot freely deploy the prohibited alternatives. Biosphere maintenance supports continued habitation; it does not establish an individual guarantee of food, shelter or care, so guarantees remain unresolved. Useful farming, craft, government and other human activity stays visible, and preindustrial life provides no all-person nonworking census. The record describes the actual restrictive period, without promoting the original colony plan or a later negotiated solution into an unverified provision system.',
 [None,-.95,None],[None,[-1,-.75],None],
 ['Actual nanotechnological ecosystem support coexists with enforced destruction of advanced human technology and continuing preindustrial labor.','Autonomous Winds determine the permitted technological ceiling despite local human aristocracies.',nw],refs,6,zero=True))
