R.append(scoped_record('c0816','lockstep-individual-robot-economy','Lockstep — Individually owned robot workforces','Lockstep','The founding-family empire’s robot-supported waking economy',['book'],
 'Lockstep novel and author’s specific robot-economy explanation','Established synchronized empire before Toby’s challenge changes its order','Living humans during active waking cycles',
 ['Hibernation calendar time as active leisure','The author’s real-world minimum-income preferences as fictional law','Political tyranny as proof that the family owns every robot'],
 'Lockstep civilizations sleep for long intervals while robots prepare food, repair environments and maintain settlements for the next waking cycle. The author explains a distinctive ownership rule: individuals hold general robot workforces and receive their earnings, whereas corporations may own only specialized machines. This is actual technological production supporting human consumption and income without equivalent personal labor.\n\nProductive assets are meaningfully dispersed among individuals, giving control a favorable distributed-human estimate. That differs from political sovereignty: the founding family can weaponize hibernation access and impose severe exclusion. Guarantees are consequently uncertain and placed slightly toward the weak side, with a wide interval for ordinarily prosperous support versus coercive loss of the system. The record does not infer an unconditional basic-income law from the author’s separate real-world policy discussion. Nonworking remains null because decades asleep are not active leisure, and residents can still trade, govern, create, care and perform useful work when awake.',
 [.25,.65,None],[[-.55,.8],[.3,.9],None],
 ['Robots supply food and maintain settlements, while individual owners receive robot-workforce profits; access can be coercively restricted through the cycle system.','The author explicitly disperses general robot ownership among individuals, while the founding family’s political power remains a major qualification.','No awake-population census exists; long hibernation intervals must not be converted to a nonworking percentage.'],refs,4,alternatives=[2]))
