R.append(scoped_record('c0818','polity-earth-pre-quiet-war','Polity — Earth before the Quiet War','Gridlinked / Polity background','Machine industry and state-supported humans under corporate-political elites',['book'],
 'Neal Asher’s Polity setting encyclopedia, Earth Central historical entry','Established Earth economy before the Quiet War and autonomous AI takeover','Living human Earth residents',
 ['Post-Quiet War AI sovereignty','Every colony as having the same benefits','State handouts as a verified comprehensive necessities charter'],
 'Before the Quiet War, most industry is already run by machines and much of the lower-class population depends on state handouts. The Earth Central computer administers budgets, taxes and services for the corporate-political class. This establishes an implemented automation-and-support economy rather than a future plan. Guarantees receive only a modest favorable estimate because support exists but its adequacy, coverage and enforceability are not established in the short author entry.\n\nEffective authority remains with human politicians and corporate leaders, who direct the administrative machine and concentrate economic power. Control therefore sits near the human-elite position. The later AI takeover is a materially different period, not retroactively the sovereign of this earlier order. Benefit dependence also does not measure all useful activity: people can still provide care, culture, research or informal services. Nonworking remains unresolved. The point is narrowly historical Earth, without extending its precise institutions to every Polity colony or interpreting the entry’s polemical portrayal as a neutral welfare census.',
 [-.2,.05,None],[[-.65,.6],[0,.2],None],
 ['The author explicitly places machine-run industry and a state-dependent majority under the prewar Earth Central administrative system.','Corporate-political human elites direct the computer and concentrate decision-making before the Quiet War.',nw],refs,1,alternatives=[3]))
